  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A loudspeaker connected to a signal generator is held over the open end of a vertical glass tube. The tube is partially filled with water to create an air column of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>, as shown in the diagram below.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The water level is gradually lowered to increase the length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span>. The first resonance occurs when <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L = 17.0\\text{ cm}\"></span> and the second resonance occurs when <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L = 51.0\\text{ cm}\"></span>. The speed of sound in the air column is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"340\\text{ m s}^{-1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the frequency produced by the signal generator?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"250\\text{ Hz}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"500\\text{ Hz}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1000\\text{ Hz}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2000\\text{ Hz}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
